    "q-88765": {
      "dom_id": "step-q88765",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The point $(4,7)$ is stretched in $x$-direction and factor $-2,$ and then stretched in the $y$-direction and factor $-1.$ What is the resulting point?",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply the given transformation.\n\n- A stretch in the $x$-direction of factor $-2$ can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(-2x,y).\n$$\n\n- A stretch in the $y$-direction of factor $-1$ can be represented by the function\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(x,-y).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the combination of the stretches is given by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(-2x,-1y).\n$$\n\nApplying the combined stretch to our point, we obtain\n\n$$\n(4,7)↦(-2\\cdot 4,\\,-1\\cdot 7)=(-8,-7).\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14275005/assets/19c76863d500606caf192378e2224e101265f0e26ab7a976c014ccd1dbc24d4e.png)",
